.TH SDL_AttachVirtualJoystick 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_AttachVirtualJoystick \- Attach a new virtual joystick.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_JoystickID SDL_AttachVirtualJoystick(const SDL_VirtualJoystickDesc *desc);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apps can create virtual joysticks, that exist without hardware directly backing them, and have program-supplied inputs\[char46] Once attached, a virtual joystick looks like any other joystick that SDL can access\[char46] These can be used to make other things look like joysticks, or provide pre-recorded input, etc\[char46]
.PP
Once attached, the app can send joystick inputs to the new virtual joystick using
.BR SDL_SetJoystickVirtualAxis (),
etc\[char46]
.PP
When no longer needed, the virtual joystick can be removed by calling
.BR SDL_DetachVirtualJoystick ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I desc
joystick description, initialized using
.BR SDL_INIT_INTERFACE ()\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the joystick instance ID, or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

